      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO ADJECTIVES"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Adjectives modify nouns/pronouns and follow strict positional and ordering rules (e.g., OSASCOMP structure) essential for SSC exams.",
        "Degrees of comparison include positive, comparative, and superlative forms with specific rules for regular and irregular adjectives.",
        "Crucial quantifier distinctions exist between countable usages (Few, Fewer, Many) and uncountable usages (Little, Less, Much).",
        "Structural patterns such as 'As...As', 'So...That', 'Too...To', and 'Enough' are heavily tested in sentence improvement.",
        "Confusables like 'Later vs. Latter' and 'Elder vs. Older' require clear distinction between time/position and relationship/age."
      ],
      "id": "zxagp7q"
    },
