      "content": "19. ADJECTIVES THAT LOOK LIKE ADVERBS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vcxlsdp"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Spotting errors in 'Few / A Few / The Few' (Countable) vs. 'Little / A Little / The Little' (Uncountable) is a top SSC favorite.",
        "Watch out for double comparatives or double superlatives (e.g., 'more wiser' or 'most tallest'), which are common examination traps.",
        "'Elder' is used exclusively for family relationships without 'than', whereas 'Older' is followed by 'than' for general age comparisons.",
        "The modifier 'Enough' always comes AFTER the adjective it modifies (e.g., 'smart enough', not 'enough smart')."
      ],
      "id": "1mb0wpt"
    },
